<b><i>Orange</i></b>

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:29.190
<i><b>10% Fruit Juice</b></i>

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.200
Are you sure that's the right choice?

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:36.220
I suppose you wouldn't know how 
to use a drink fountain, would you?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:40.760
Given your lack of friends, what occasion 
have you to visit a restaurant like this?

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.420
I could say the same to you.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.530
Allow me to demonstrate.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:46.860
<b>Refreshing White Grape</b>

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:46.860
<b>20% Fruit Juice</b>

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.530
You watching?

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.000
<b>Orange</b>

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.000
<b>10% Fruit Juice</b>

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.760
When using the drink fountain,

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.630
Melon Flavor    Contains no juice

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:54.760
one is supposed to mix 
the drinks together like so

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.390
and create one's own unique blend.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:02.300
Are you... for real?

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.150
Now it's your turn to try. 
Let your heart lead the way.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.440
Bring it on!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.350
Sorry, Yume-chan!

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.420
I wasn't serious when I said 
to mix the drinks at the fountain.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:18.490
It was a joke!

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.060
Are you... serious right now?

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.040
Looks like you got Mizuto fooled too!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.440
Wow, like peas in a pod!

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.050
It's almost like you two are siblings!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.340
Like you two bosom buddies can talk!

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.370
That was great!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.630
Say, Irido-kun.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.100
You're good at Japanese, right?

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:45.190
Mind tutoring me later?

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.190
Midterms are coming up, you know?

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:49.150
Is the snuggling necessary?

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:53.620
I gotta make Yume-chan so jealous that
 she begs me to snuggle up to her instead.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.440
That's just plain dirty.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.660
If you need a tutor,
 you should ask her instead.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:01.790
Me?

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:07.080
Yeah. You're better suited 
to teaching than I'll ever be.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.420
So dedicated to your studies.

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.380
How smart of you to notice.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.320
Of course!

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.520
You actually have to work hard to succeed,

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:18.480
whereas I attain good grades 
with very little effort.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.010
I'd hardly be an effective tutor.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.380
What's your problem?!

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.850
Is it your life's work to piss me off?!

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.560
Touché, Irido-kun.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.780
Didn't think you'd take advantage of 
the situation to one-up me like that.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:43.950
All Irido's been doing is studying for midterms. 
I'm so bored! So much for "very little effort"

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:43.950
Read

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.710
Akatsuki

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.710
Huh? Aren't you studying too, Kawanami?
 Me and Yume-chan are

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:51.340
Yume

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:51.340
Kawanami-kun, we don't go to just any old school. 
Think back on how hard the entrance exam was

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.450
Say, Irido...

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.850
How hard do you think exams are...

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:56.890
Hard.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:01.810
So hard that someone like me, who prides 
himself on not trying, actually has to try.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.140
For real?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.290
For real.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:11.610
So the freedom I was promised 
after I got in was all a lie!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:16.860
Well, I suppose you don't have to try 
if you're okay with any old passing grade.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.250
Huh?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.330
So why are you studying so hard, Irido?

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.500
I can't go losing to my little sister, can I?

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.090
You two are something else.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:36.320
I've never felt compelled to 
face off with someone like that.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.370
Really?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:42.140
From what I saw today, you two 
seemed pretty competitive to me.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:48.030
But we're too concerned about appearances 
to butt heads as openly as you do.

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.760
I'm exhausted just thinking 
about keeping that up.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:55.480
The way I see it, at least you 
two have some sense of decorum.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.760
The grass is always greener 
on the other side, I guess.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.780
Look at you, spouting proverbs. 
And you were worried about studying.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:07.180
When life gives you lemons, 
make lemonade, right?

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.740
Now that I think about it,

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:15.560
it might be nice to do better than Minami.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.820
That's the spirit. You got this.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.680
That was your invitation 
to tutor me, Mr. Smartypants!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.820
In case of emergency, break this wall and 
escape through the neighboring apartment

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.650
In case of emergency, break this wall and 
escape through the neighboring apartment

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:52.990
Are you really that embarrassed 
I caught you standing there gaping?

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.840
Do you really have to state the obvious?!

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:59.510
I never knew you were into 
wearing such cutesy pajamas.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.780
It must be tough holding back with me around.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.840
I'm only wearing this because 
Akatsuki-san forced me to!

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:10.540
It's okay, it's okay. I think it's cute.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.350
In a dorky way.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.020
I heard that!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.570
The moon is beautiful, isn't it?

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.050
You remember? That time on the school trip?

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.180
Like I could forget.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:36.500
Not after somebody dared 
to use such a pretentious come-on.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:40.420
It's bad form to harp on a 
man's youthful indiscretions.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:46.360
What would you do if I told you 
that's when I started liking you?

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.940
There'd be no point.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.790
What would it change?

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:53.070
You're right.

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:56.350
I wouldn't call what I felt 
back then "liking you" anyway.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:58.680
But you did feel something?

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.480
Forget I said anything.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:06.940
Why bring that up all of a sudden anyway?

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.300
No reason.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:14.280
It's just... Akatsuki-san and Kawanami-kun
 today had me thinking.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:18.560
I wonder if there's meaning in all 
that time they've spent together.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:21.220
All that time, huh?

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.650
I'm sure those two would have 
things to say about that.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:30.790
It's not like you and I have to go out of 
our way to spend time together anyway.

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:34.890
As long as our parents stay together, that is.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.480
You think they'll ever split up?

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:42.970
Not really.

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:47.990
I think we're stuck as stepsiblings 
until the end of time.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.070
Kinda sucks, doesn't it?

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.490
You're telling me.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.870
Did you have fun today?

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:02.150
Yeah, thanks.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.020
You're welcome.
